data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_0b39e835db4dce60006a70f90b735881958d4632e5218ffaf8","logprobs":[],"output_index":2,"sequence_number":143,"text":"Here’s what’s **newest today (Monday, August 3, 2026)** around **Azure AI** (including Microsoft Foundry / Azure AI platform news), based on Microsoft’s own update feeds and recent official posts:\n\n## Today’s most “current” Azure update signals\n- **Azure service updates continue to roll in on the Azure Updates feed** (Microsoft’s central changelog). If you filter that page for AI-related services (Foundry, Azure AI Search, Azure OpenAI/Models, API Management, Databricks, etc.), you’ll see the freshest GA/preview items as they publish. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/updates/))  \n- A third-party consolidated tracker that mirrors official sources is already showing **new items posted today (Aug 3, 2026)** in the Azure updates stream (useful for quick scanning by date). ([azurecharts.com](https://azurecharts.com/updates?monthback=0))  \n\n## Recent (late July / early July) Azure AI–relevant announcements that are still “breaking” in practice\n- **GPT-5.6 is now available in Microsoft Foundry** (Azure blog announcement dated **July 9, 2026**). This is one of the most directly “Azure AI platform” model-availability announcements from Microsoft recently. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/))  \n- **Claude is generally available in Microsoft Foundry** (Azure blog announcement dated **June 29, 2026**), positioning Foundry as a multi-model platform hosted on Azure. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/))  \n- **Microsoft Foundry June 2026 roundup** (posted **July 7, 2026**) includes platform/agent updates like agent publishing paths and other Foundry capabilities that matter if you’re building agentic apps on Azure. ([devblogs.microsoft.com](https://devblogs.microsoft.com/foundry/whats-new-in-microsoft-foundry-june-2026/))  \n- In **Azure Updates (July 2026)**, Microsoft lists **“AI Gateway tier in Azure API Management” in public preview**, aimed at governing/exposing AI assets (models, MCP servers, tools) with policy, auth, and observability—very relevant to operationalizing Azure AI securely. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/updates/))  \n\n## “News” framing from the broader market (not product release notes)\n- Several outlets are tying Microsoft’s recent earnings/market moves to **Azure + AI demand** (this is more business news than hands-on Azure AI feature news, but it’s what’s being covered “today”). ([usatoday.com](https://www.usatoday.com/story/money/business/2026/07/31/microsoft-stock-record-one-day-gain/91126672007/))  \n\nIf you tell me what you mean by “Azure AI” (e.g., **Foundry**, **Azure OpenAI/model catalog**, **Azure AI Search**, **Azure ML**, **Vision/Speech**, **agent building**, or **governance/security**), I can pull the **exact newest items from the Azure Updates feed for that slice** and summarize them."}

